pg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">From ancestral memory to digital desire, from queer ecologies to fragile landscapes, ten artists’ films explore resistance, love and transformation in the present tense.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/perfect-blue-4k-restoration\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Perfect Blue (4K Restoration)</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">1:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11850.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">After leaving her pop idol group and starting a new life as an actress, Mima soon finds herself overwhelmed by a wave of provocative roles that go against her wishes. Before long, a string of murders begins to unfold, targeting those around her…</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-dreams\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Dreams</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">3:40 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11813.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">From Mexican director Michel Franco comes a chilling drama about the underbelly of philanthropy, where the assuaging of guilt is compromised by sexual desire.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-duse\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Duse</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11812.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Pietro Marcello’s mesmerising biopic charts the later life of Eleanor Duse, Italy’s greatest actress of the early 20th century.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/pace-peter-hujars-day\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Peter Hujar's Day + Q&A with Ben Whishaw</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11935.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Ben Whishaw and Rebecca Hall star in the masterful new film from Ira Sachs, an intimate, richly cinematic rendering of a conversation between photographer Peter Hujar and writer Linda Rosenkrantz.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-back-and-forth-across-the-line\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Back and Forth Across the Line</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11867.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">This programme of films interrogates a myriad of borders. Some are physical, geo-politically determined, others are socially inscribed. Many more are difficult to define. All are porous, even when it seems they’re not.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/souleymanes-story\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Souleymane's Story</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">9:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11994.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Every second of Souleymane’s new life in France is precious. Having fled Guinea, his asylum interview looms. He powers through the streets of after dark Paris as a delivery rider, sleeps in hostels and prepares for his make-or-break appointment.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item talks \"><div class=\"subhead sans talks\">\n                                              <a href=\"/talks\">Talks & Engagement</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/talks/the-toe-rag-launch-party\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Toe Rag Launch Party <br> Issue 7: The Pastoral</div></div><div class=\"time-container time talks\">7:00 PM</div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12075.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Join The Toe Rag to celebrate the forthcoming ‘Pastoral’ issue. Artist Nina Coulson is offering a four-leaf clover with every magazine.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Saturday, 18 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Saturday, 18 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/frieze-x-ica-film-programme-2025\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Frieze × ICA Artists' Film Programme 2025 </div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12060.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">From ancestral memory to digital desire, from queer ecologies to fragile landscapes, ten artists’ films explore resistance, love and transformation in the present tense.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">1:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11808.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Prolific Romanian provocateur Radu Jude returns with a sharp social satire on our materialistic society, blending dark comedy, drama and giant, plastic dinosaurs.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/a-want-in-her\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">A Want In Her</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11984.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">When her mother goes missing somewhere in Ireland, artist Myrid Carten returns from London to find her. Her search takes her into a feuding family, a contested house; and a history that threatens to take everyone down, including herself.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-cadences-of-refusal\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Cadences of Refusal</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11866.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Activated by political urgency and defiance, these five works envision a collective reimagining and remaking of the world. Each crafts a counter-grammar to traditional non-fiction cinema – grounded in poetry, fragmentation, inquiry and the voice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/happyend\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Happyend</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:10 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11873.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Set in a dystopian near-future Tokyo, Neo Sora’s striking debut feature follows a group of teenagers challenging the rigid expectations of society.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-afterlives\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Afterlives</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:15 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11863.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Media artist, filmmaker and critic Kevin B. Lee presents an unflinchingly complex and thought-provoking tapestry that interrogates the many faces of violence confronting our lives.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/souleymanes-story\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Souleymane's Story</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11994.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Every second of Souleymane’s new life in France is precious. Having fled Guinea, his asylum interview looms. He powers through the streets of after dark Paris as a delivery rider, sleeps in hostels and prepares for his make-or-break appointment.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/the-art-of-this\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">In the Round: the Art of This</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11793.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">The Art of This, an off shoot, a descendant, a sub-set of electronic pioneers Art of Noise, make their performance debut at ICA. This show will feature words, music and images by Art of This, Art of Noise and the art of others, and will be a performance in the round, using the venue's 360° spatial soundsystem, d&amp;b Soundscape.&nbsp;<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-what-marielle-knows\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">What Marielle Knows </div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11811.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">This sharply observed and darkly comic tale of familial relations will leave you rolling in the aisles and perhaps reassessing your own bond with your loved ones.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Sunday, 19 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Sunday, 19 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/frieze-x-ica-film-programme-2025\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Frieze × ICA Artists' Film Programme 2025 </div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12060.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">From ancestral memory to digital desire, from queer ecologies to fragile landscapes, ten artists’ films explore resistance, love and transformation in the present tense.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-anatomy-of-place-sites-of-becoming\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Anatomy of Place, Sites of Becoming</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">1:10 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11862.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Films in this programme consider how spaces hold the weight of what came before and the traces of what may emerge, moving through landscapes where memory, body and terrain shifts and transforms against time.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/a-want-in-her\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">A Want In Her</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11984.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">When her mother goes missing somewhere in Ireland, artist Myrid Carten returns from London to find her. Her search takes her into a feuding family, a contested house; and a history that threatens to take everyone down, including herself.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-in-the-clouds-flecks-of-memories-pass\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">In the Clouds Flecks of Memories Pass </div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">3:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11860.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">These films embody memories: some personal, others inherited or found. At times they’re mesmerising, yet fissures can appear in the depicted recollections. Subjectivity comes into focus. Established narratives are destabilised.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-with-hasan-in-gaza\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">With Hasan in Gaza</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">5:40 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11809.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Kamal Aljafari returns with a poignant reimagining of Palestinian history – a profound meditation on absence and loss, crafted with quiet integrity.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/souleymanes-story\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Souleymane's Story</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11994.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Every second of Souleymane’s new life in France is precious. Having fled Guinea, his asylum interview looms. He powers through the streets of after dark Paris as a delivery rider, sleeps in hostels and prepares for his make-or-break appointment.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/perfect-blue-4k-restoration\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Perfect Blue (4K Restoration)</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:15 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11850.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">After leaving her pop idol group and starting a new life as an actress, Mima soon finds herself overwhelmed by a wave of provocative roles that go against her wishes. Before long, a string of murders begins to unfold, targeting those around her…</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lff-nouvelle-vague\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">BFI London Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Nouvelle Vague</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:25 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11810.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Richard Linklater recreates the making of Jean-Luc Godard’s seminal feature debut, penning a nostalgic love letter to the rebellious spirit of the French New Wave.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Monday, 20 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Monday, 20 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class='item other'><div class='title'>The ICA is closed on Mondays.</div></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Tuesday, 21 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Tuesday, 21 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/souleymanes-story\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Souleymane's Story</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11994.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Every second of Souleymane’s new life in France is precious. Having fled Guinea, his asylum interview looms. He powers through the streets of after dark Paris as a delivery rider, sleeps in hostels and prepares for his make-or-break appointment.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Wednesday, 22 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Wednesday, 22 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/tanoa-sasraku-film-club-there-will-be-blood\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Artist's Film Club: <br>There Will Be Blood</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11728.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Paul Thomas Anderson's sprawling epic about family, faith and power, centres upon Daniel Day-Lewis's Machiavellian silver minor turned oil prospector, during California's turn-of-the-century petroleum boom. Selected by Tanoa Sasraku to accompany her exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item talks \"><div class=\"subhead sans talks\">\n                                              <a href=\"/talks\">Talks & Engagement</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/talks/book-launch-performance-nymph-by-stephanie-la-cava\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Book Launch + Performance <br> Nymph by Stephanie LaCava </div></div><div class=\"time-container time talks\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12004.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Join us for an evening of performance and conversation to celebrate the launch of Stephanie LaCava’s new novel <i>Nymph</i>. &nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/souleymanes-story\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Souleymane's Story</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">9:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11994.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Every second of Souleymane’s new life in France is precious. Having fled Guinea, his asylum interview looms. He powers through the streets of after dark Paris as a delivery rider, sleeps in hostels and prepares for his make-or-break appointment.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Thursday, 23 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Thursday, 23 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/souleymanes-story\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Souleymane's Story</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11994.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Every second of Souleymane’s new life in France is precious. Having fled Guinea, his asylum interview looms. He powers through the streets of after dark Paris as a delivery rider, sleeps in hostels and prepares for his make-or-break appointment.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/angelopoulos-reconstruction\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">Opening Night </br>Reconstruction</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11503.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A striking fusion of documentary, drama, and myth, Angelopoulos debut feature is a haunting tragedy that draws from both Aeschylus' Oresteia trilogy and film noir to reconstruct a crime and its consequences.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/holden-zimpel\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">In the Round: Holden & Zimpel</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11306.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Holden &amp; Zimpel perform in the round at ICA, using the venue's 360° spatial soundsystem system, d&amp;b Soundscape.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/perfect-blue-4k-restoration\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Perfect Blue (4K Restoration)</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11850.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">After leaving her pop idol group and starting a new life as an actress, Mima soon finds herself overwhelmed by a wave of provocative roles that go against her wishes. Before long, a string of murders begins to unfold, targeting those around her…</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Friday, 24 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Friday, 24 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-mastermind\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Mastermind</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:35 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">9:10 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11937.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a sedate Massachusetts suburb circa 1970, unemployed family man and amateur art thief J.B Mooney sets out on his first heist. With the museum cased and accomplices recruited, he has an airtight plan.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/love-war\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Love+War</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12054.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sensitive documentary following Pulitzer winner Lynsey Addario, a conflict photographer balancing dangerous assignments with motherhood and deep personal sacrifice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-levers\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br> Levers + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11958.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Filmed on broken Bolex cameras and developed from a script of loose poetry, <i>Levers</i> traces a series of oneiric encounters in the Red River Valley following a sudden blackout after the unveiling of a new sculpture.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Saturday, 25 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Saturday, 25 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-mastermind\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Mastermind</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">12:00 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11937.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a sedate Massachusetts suburb circa 1970, unemployed family man and amateur art thief J.B Mooney sets out on his first heist. With the museum cased and accomplices recruited, he has an airtight plan.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/days-of-36\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">Days of '36</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11505.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Theo Angelopoulos' second feature, and the first part of his trilogy of history, <i>Days of '36</i> leans further into the procedural tendencies of his debut as he crafts a densely layered investigation into the machinations of political corruption.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-levers\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br> Levers + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11958.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Filmed on broken Bolex cameras and developed from a script of loose poetry, <i>Levers</i> traces a series of oneiric encounters in the Red River Valley following a sudden blackout after the unveiling of a new sculpture.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/jukebox-film-club-married-to-music-q-a\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Married to the Music + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12028.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">The explosive new documentary from director Garo Berberian, charts the wild rise of dance music — from its birth in the gay black clubs of Chicago, through Manchester’s acid house revolution, the outlawed days of illegal raves and pirate radio.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/mermaid-chunky\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">In the Round: Mermaid Chunky </div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11355.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Mermaid Chunky. It’s all in a name, sometimes. The danceable, costumed, curiosity rich duo of artists Freya Tate and Moina Moin are as imaginative as they profess. Or, to get more to the point, as we all need them to be. They perform as part of our in-the-round spatial series this October.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/love-war\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Love+War</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:40 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12054.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sensitive documentary following Pulitzer winner Lynsey Addario, a conflict photographer balancing dangerous assignments with motherhood and deep personal sacrifice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Sunday, 26 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Sunday, 26 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-mastermind\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Mastermind</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">12:00 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">8:15 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11937.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a sedate Massachusetts suburb circa 1970, unemployed family man and amateur art thief J.B Mooney sets out on his first heist. With the museum cased and accomplices recruited, he has an airtight plan.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-travelling-players\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">The Travelling Players</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11506.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sweeping journey through Greek history and an intimate epic of love and death, Angelopoulos landmark film follows the travails of a travelling theatre troupe, as they are swept along by the bloody tides of history from Nazi occupation to civil war.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-levers\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br> Levers + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11958.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Filmed on broken Bolex cameras and developed from a script of loose poetry, <i>Levers</i> traces a series of oneiric encounters in the Red River Valley following a sudden blackout after the unveiling of a new sculpture.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/love-war\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Love+War</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12054.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sensitive documentary following Pulitzer winner Lynsey Addario, a conflict photographer balancing dangerous assignments with motherhood and deep personal sacrifice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Monday, 27 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Monday, 27 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class