exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-mastermind\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Mastermind</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:20 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11937.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a sedate Massachusetts suburb circa 1970, unemployed family man and amateur art thief J.B Mooney sets out on his first heist. With the museum cased and accomplices recruited, he has an airtight plan.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/love-war\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Love+War</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">5:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12054.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sensitive documentary following Pulitzer winner Lynsey Addario, a conflict photographer balancing dangerous assignments with motherhood and deep personal sacrifice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/preview-belen-q-a\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">PREVIEW Belén + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12079.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">The true story that sparked an international movement, chronicling the harrowing case of Julieta, a woman falsely accused of infanticide, and Soledad Deza, the fearless lawyer who takes on the highly controversial case.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-levers\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br> Levers + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11958.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Filmed on broken Bolex cameras and developed from a script of loose poetry, <i>Levers</i> traces a series of oneiric encounters in the Red River Valley following a sudden blackout after the unveiling of a new sculpture.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Wednesday, 29 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Wednesday, 29 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-mastermind\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Mastermind</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:15 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">8:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11937.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a sedate Massachusetts suburb circa 1970, unemployed family man and amateur art thief J.B Mooney sets out on his first heist. With the museum cased and accomplices recruited, he has an airtight plan.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/love-war\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Love+War</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">5:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12054.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sensitive documentary following Pulitzer winner Lynsey Addario, a conflict photographer balancing dangerous assignments with motherhood and deep personal sacrifice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-levers\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br> Levers + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11958.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Filmed on broken Bolex cameras and developed from a script of loose poetry, <i>Levers</i> traces a series of oneiric encounters in the Red River Valley following a sudden blackout after the unveiling of a new sculpture.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item talks \"><div class=\"subhead sans talks\">\n                                              <a href=\"/talks\">Talks & Engagement</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/talks/speaking-futures-on-artist-collectives\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Speaking Futures <br> On Artist Collectives: Diasporas Now × Resolve × B.O.S.S. </div></div><div class=\"time-container time talks\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12087.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Why do we need artist collectives and how do they form? Join us for the next event in the Speaking Futures x Diasporas Now programme: an evening of conversation exploring artist collectives.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/titanic\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">In the Round: Titanic</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11338.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">As part of a series of In the Round shows this October, Titanic, the chamber-jazz-meets-art-pop collaboration between Mabe Fratti and I La Catolica, will perform live using the venue's 360° spatial soundsystem, d&amp;b Soundscape.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/doc-n-roll-nash-the-slash-rises-again-q-a\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">Doc'n Roll Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Doc'n Roll: Nash The Slash Rises Again! + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:40 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11738.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the late 1970s, Nash the Slash emerged as one of music’s true enigmas, an electric violinist and sonic alchemist blending classical finesse with punk rebellion. From scoring Un Chien Andalou live to mesmerizing audiences with his analog arsenal, Nash pushed the boundaries of performance and sound.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Thursday, 30 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Thursday, 30 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-mastermind\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">The Mastermind</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:10 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">8:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11937.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a sedate Massachusetts suburb circa 1970, unemployed family man and amateur art thief J.B Mooney sets out on his first heist. With the museum cased and accomplices recruited, he has an airtight plan.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/love-war\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Love+War</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">5:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12054.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A sensitive documentary following Pulitzer winner Lynsey Addario, a conflict photographer balancing dangerous assignments with motherhood and deep personal sacrifice.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-levers\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br> Levers + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11958.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Filmed on broken Bolex cameras and developed from a script of loose poetry, <i>Levers</i> traces a series of oneiric encounters in the Red River Valley following a sudden blackout after the unveiling of a new sculpture.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/doc-n-roll-a-way-to-die-the-short-films-of-coil-online-q-a\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">Doc'n Roll Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Doc'n Roll: A Way to Die: The Short-films of Coil + online Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:40 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11739.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">After paying tribute to and introducing the photographic and pictorial work of Peter Christopherson (1955-2010) and John Balance (1962-2004) to a larger audience, founding members of the cult formation COIL, Timeless editions have had the duo’s filmed archives restored.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Friday, 31 October</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Friday, 31 October</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:20 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12033.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the capital of Transylvania, Cluj-Napoca, Orsolya works as a bailiff. She has to evict a homeless guy from a cellar one day, which has disastrous results.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Saturday, 1 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Saturday, 1 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">12:30 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12033.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the capital of Transylvania, Cluj-Napoca, Orsolya works as a bailiff. She has to evict a homeless guy from a cellar one day, which has disastrous results.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/the-hunters\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">The Hunters</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">3:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11507.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">History is upended as a bourgeois New Years Eve party is thrown into disarray by the discovery of a rebel soldiers corpse seemingly from the Greek Civil War more than twenty-five years prior. An exorcism of the personal and collective ills of a nation, <i>The Hunters</i> is a haunting coda to Theo Angelopoulos' trilogy of history.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/in-the-realm-of-acting-uk-premiere-the-written-face\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">In the Realm of Acting: <br>Performance On and Off Screen</div><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE <br>The Written Face (4K Restoration)</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11772.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A fantastical exploration of performance, <i>The Written Face</i> drifts through the twilight between reality and dreams, drawing out the artistic philosophies of kabuki star Bando Tamasaburo V and other legends like Kazuo Ohno, captured with Daniel Schmid’s singular aesthetic vision.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/seefeel\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Seefeel + James Massiah</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11461.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Unconcerned with trends and always pushing forward, Seefeel remain icons of experimentation— blurring the boundaries between guitar music and electronic music - pioneers of a sound that has only grown more vital and influential with time. Support from James Massiah.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Sunday, 2 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Sunday, 2 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">12:00 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">5:50 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12033.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the capital of Transylvania, Cluj-Napoca, Orsolya works as a bailiff. She has to evict a homeless guy from a cellar one day, which has disastrous results.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/alexander-the-great\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">Alexander the Great</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11508.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">With his fifth feature, Theo Angelopoulos turns to the dawn of the twentieth century for a politically charged fable centred upon the leader of a revolutionary commune, who causes an international incident when he takes a group of British aristocrats hostage.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/big-brave\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">BIG|BRAVE</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11016.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">The Montreal, Quebec trio BIG | BRAVE create heavy, vast post-rock. Minimalism, structural freedom and meticulous timing form the cornerstones of their precise, rhythmical sound. Support from Sealionwoman.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Monday, 3 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Monday, 3 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class='item other'><div class='title'>The ICA is closed on Mondays.</div></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Tuesday, 4 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Tuesday, 4 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:10 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12033.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the capital of Transylvania, Cluj-Napoca, Orsolya works as a bailiff. She has to evict a homeless guy from a cellar one day, which has disastrous results.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-in-conversation\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku in conversation with Rosalind Nashashibi </div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11735.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Join us for an insightful conversation about the development of Sasraku’s work in the context of her new show at the ICA.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/phew\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Phew + Isaiah Hull + Freddie Murphy</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11184.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Phew is a legendary figure in Japanese underground music and was a founding member of the legendary Japanese punk band Aunt Sally. Supported by Freddie Murphy, a sound artist and curator based in Torino, Italy.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/doc-n-roll-pieces-of-heaven-porridge-radio-q-a\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">Doc'n Roll Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Doc'n Roll: Pieces of Heaven: Porridge Radio + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11740.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A spellbinding farewell from Porridge Radio, Pieces Of Heaven was filmed at the Centre Pompidou in 2024 to mark the release of the band’s final album, <i>Clouds In The Sky They Will Always Be There For Me</i>. Led by songwriter Dana Margolin, it moves through inertia, heartbreak and dysphoria as she distils over a decade of music into one unforgettable hour.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Wednesday, 5 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Wednesday, 5 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:15 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12033.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the capital of Transylvania, Cluj-Napoca, Orsolya works as a bailiff. She has to evict a homeless guy from a cellar one day, which has disastrous results.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/nabeel\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Nabeel (نبيل)</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11688.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Nabeel is a band, formed by Iraqi-American musician Yasir Razak, blending indie shoegaze and DIY bedroom band energy with the sounds of his Arabic roots.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Thursday, 6 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Thursday, 6 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/kontinental-25\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Kontinental '25</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">3:15 PM</div><div class=\"time-slot\">6:20 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12033.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In the capital of Transylvania, Cluj-Napoca, Orsolya works as a bailiff. She has to evict a homeless guy from a cellar one day, which has disastrous results.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lkff-the-meryl-streep-project\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">London Korean Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">The Meryl Streep Project</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12035.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Director Park Hyo-sun’s eight-year documentary blends her admiration for Meryl Streep with a feminist reflection on young Korean women’s struggles, dreams, and solidarity.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/los-thuthanaka\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Los Thuthanaka</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11456.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Los Thuthanaka (founded by West Coast artists Chuquimamani-Condori and Joshua Chuquimia Crampton) bridges the past, present and future of the mighty Pakajaqui Nation through a potent blend of Andean rhythms, Aymara composition and psychedelic rock to create a style of Andean music unheard until now.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/angelopoulos-athens\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">Athens, Return to the Acropolis + Broadcast</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:40 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11504.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Commissioned for a television series on Europe's cultural capitals, Theo Angelopoulos' ode to the city of Athens draws from the poetry of George Seferis, the music of Manos Hadjidakis and the paintings of Tsarouchis. Preceded by Angelopoulos' first completed film <i>Broadcast</i>.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Friday, 7 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Friday, 7 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-fantaisie\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br>Fantaisie + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11957.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Lost in her fears and fantasies, a young woman writes in a notebook. A young man finds this notebook on a train. Suddenly, they find themselves in the heart of a forest, in a nocturnal reality where dreams come to life in Isabel Pagliai’s first feature.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item live \"><div class=\"subhead sans live\">\n                                              <a href=\"/live\">Live</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/live/sorry\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Sorry: COSPLAYOGRAPHY</div></div><div class=\"time-container time live\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12067.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Composed of best friends and co-conspirators Asha and Louis, joined by drummer Lincoln Barrett, multi-instrumentalist Campbell Baum, and Marco Pini on electronics, Sorry have created their own distinctive musical world - one that draws together a shared passion for lo-fi sounds of grunge, trap, and shoegaze.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lkff-the-good-the-bad-the-weird\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">London Korean Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">The Good, the Bad, the Weird</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">8:45 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12036.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A thrilling “Manchurian Western” blending action, history, and genre spectacle with lasting impact.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Saturday, 8 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Saturday, 8 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/ba-a-sudden-glimpse-to-deeper-things\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">A Sudden Glimpse to Deeper Things</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">2:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11709.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A special screening of Mark Cousins documentary which dives into the life and art of Wilhelmina Barns-Graham, a visionary 20th-century artist who saw the natural world in extraordinary ways. Preceded by an introduction from Professor Annette Kuhn FBA.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/in-the-realm-of-acting-stendali-still-they-toll-jane-b-for-agnes-v\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">In the Realm of Acting: <br>Performance On and Off Screen</div><div class=\"title \">Stendalì: Still They Toll + <br>Jane B. for Agnès V (2K Restoration)</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11784.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">A collaboration between Cecilia Mangini and Pier Paolo Pasolini, recording a vanishing female mourning ritual in Southern Italy meditating on culturally coded expressions of grief and collective memory, screens with Agnès Varda's imaginary biopic of Jane Birkin unveiling multiple Janes, both cultural icon and a woman.&nbsp;</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lkff-time-to-be-strong\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">London Korean Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">Time to Be Strong</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12037.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Three former K-pop idols reunite on Jeju Island, confronting past traumas, lost youth, and the scars of an exploitative industry in a tender journey.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lkff-the-land-of-morning-calm\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">London Korean Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">The Land of Morning Calm</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12038.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">In a fading coastal village, a bitter old fisherman harbors dark secrets, revealing a haunting portrait of loss, survival, and lives left behind.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-fantaisie\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br>Fantaisie + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">6:30 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11957.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Lost in her fears and fantasies, a young woman writes in a notebook. A young man finds this notebook on a train. Suddenly, they find themselves in the heart of a forest, in a nocturnal reality where dreams come to life in Isabel Pagliai’s first feature.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Sunday, 9 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Sunday, 9 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class=\"other sans programme-header\">Daily Programme</div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/tanoa-sasraku-morale-patch\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Tanoa Sasraku: Morale Patch</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11857.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\"><i>Morale Patch</i> is an exhibition of new work by Tanoa Sasraku (b. 1995, Plymouth) examining the seductive and destructive power of oil – its ties to war and national identity – through a meditation on emblems and mementos.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/off-circuit-fantaisie\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">UK PREMIERE</br>Fantaisie + Q&A</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11957.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">Lost in her fears and fantasies, a young woman writes in a notebook. A young man finds this notebook on a train. Suddenly, they find themselves in the heart of a forest, in a nocturnal reality where dreams come to life in Isabel Pagliai’s first feature.<br>\r\n</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/voyage-to-cythera\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">A Moving Image of Eternity: </br>The Cinema of Theo Angelopoulos</div><div class=\"title \">Voyage to Cythera</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">4:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11509.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">The first part of his acclaimed trilogy of silence, this tale of a former resistance fighter's return to his homeland after decades in exile, marked a key transition point in Angelopoulos' work from the collective histories that preceded it to the profoundly personal films that would follow.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item films \"><div class=\"subhead sans films\">\n                                              <a href=\"/films\">Films</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/films/lkff-save\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title season-item\">London Korean Film Festival 2025</div><div class=\"title \">SAVE</div></div><div class=\"time-container time films\"><div class=\"time-slot\">7:00 PM</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/12034.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">After aging out of an orphanage, Se-jeong meets Eun-sook, an eccentric woman claiming to be her saviour — possibly a scammer, possibly her last hope.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><div class=\"item exhibitions \"><div class=\"subhead sans exhibitions\">\n                                              <a href=\"/exhibitions\">Exhibitions</a>\n                                          </div><a href=\"/exhibitions/morale-patch-film-club\"><div class=\"item-info float-container\"><div class=\"title-container\"><div class=\"title \">Morale Patch <br> Artist's Film Club</div></div></div><div class='img-container img-container-thumb'><img alt=\"\" src=\"//www.ica.art/media/11891.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>                <div class=\"description sans\">To accompany her new solo exhibition <i>Morale Patch</i>, artist Tanoa Sasraku presents four film works that connect with and expand on the show's central themes.</div>\n\t\t    </a></div><!--<div class='program sans'>Daily Program</div>--><div id='' class=\"date-title\"><div class=\"head fold\">\n        <div class=\"date-picker\">\n            <div class=\"docket-date-container\">\n                <div class=\"docket-date\">Monday, 10 November</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <!-- <div id=\"docket-date-small-header\">Monday, 10 November</div> --></div><div id = 'filter_container'>\n                                <ul id='filter-2' class = 'item'>\n                                    <li class = 'year sans '>\n                                        <a class = \"year-btn\" href = '/today' >Today</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/tomorrow'>Tomorrow</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans '>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/next-7-days'>Next 7 days</a>\n                                    </li><li class = 'year sans active'>\n                                            <a class = 'year-btn' href = '/upcoming'>Everything</a>\n                                    </li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div><div class='item other'><div class='title'>The ICA is closed on Mondays.</div></div></div>      </div>\n    </div></div>\n\n<script>\n// var endDate = \"2025-11-11\";\n// function loadMore() {\n//     document.getElementById('spinner').style.display = 'block';\n//     document.getElementById('more').style.display = 'none';\n\n//     var xhttp = new XMLHttpRequest();\n\n//     xhttp.onreadystatechange = function() {\n//       if (this.readyState == 4 && this.status == 200) {\n//         var div = document.getElementById('ladder').children[0];\n//         div.innerHTML += this.responseText;\n//         document.getElementById('spinner').style.display = 'none';\n//         document.getElementById('more'